# Git — limited agent access

## Allowed (see `git-iteration-commits.mdc`)

- Inspect: `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`
- **Granular `git add` + `git commit`** during iterations — many small commits, repo subject format

## Taboo — human unless explicitly asked

- `git push`, `pull`, `fetch`, `merge`, `rebase`, `checkout`, `branch`, cherry-pick, reset, stash (except when user directs)
- Force-push, tags, releases
- `gh pr …` and any PR/issue VCS on GitHub
- `git config` changes
- Bulk commits that mix unrelated scopes (split per iteration-commits rule)

If the user asks only for a **push** or **PR**, remind them agents commit locally; they push and open PRs.

Code edits, docs, builds, and tests are always fine.
